    "cellDiagonalDegrees": 0.353553,
    "cellDiagonalMetersAtEquator": 39225.9,
    "statement": "Natural Earth 1:50m geometry is generalized; the 50 km buffer is source-geometry seaward buffering, not an exact pixel coastline. Tile-local azimuthal-equidistant projection has sub-0.5% metric distortion across a 10-degree tile (about 250 m at 50 km at the tile edge), reported as an approximation rather than a geodesic buffer guarantee. Conservative 0.25-degree cell-footprint intersection can overreach the coastal band or underfill an excluded border by about one cell diagonal (0.3536 deg, about 39 km at the equator and 17 km at 65N)."
  },
